# Response headers for Cloudflare Pages (57-06 Task 1e).
# Read natively by the hosting, like public/_redirects - no dependency, no
# configuration, no build step.
#
# Why frame-ancestors matters here and not "some day": without it /anmeldung -
# and from Task 3 on /zugang - can be loaded invisibly inside a foreign page
# and covered with someone else's form. The visitor then types office data, or
# a password, into a page they believe is ours. X-Frame-Options says the same
# thing for older browsers that ignore the CSP directive.
#
# Deliberately NOT a full Content-Security-Policy yet: the runtime origins are
# not measured. Five map tile hosts (maplibreStyles.js:17,25,39,50,62), three
# edge functions, mapbox-gl-rtl-text.js and the language model endpoints would
# all need to be in script-src/connect-src/img-src, and a script-src that is
# one entry short breaks the app silently rather than loudly. That measurement
# is its own pass (57-06 G-13).

/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff

# Phase 78 hotfix (23.09.2026): rule sets are project material. Nothing below this
# folder may be cached at the edge - a deleted file stayed publicly cached for days.
/pruefregeln/*
  Cache-Control: no-store
